# QA M6 flow: Zuckerschock carried through Wolfgangsee -> Strobl -> Bad
# Ischl -> the Cafe Zauner intro (D-047; up to M6 it went on to the
# teaser and the title, hence the name). Title flow with the run
# started at the Wolfgangsee: START at 20, intro, then
# qa_m5_wolfgangsee_relaxed's inputs from 171 (the Mozartkugel at its
# M-box, Zuckerschock from then on, LevelComplete at 5163), idle: tally,
# route map Wolfgangsee -> Strobl, the Strobl intro and play from 6169 as
# big Resi. Strobl (clock = frame - 6169): a QA beam search (8-frame
# chunks, never hurt, power kept): the shutter staircase as big Resi, the
# Postbus, both Ampeln, the walkway, the Ache, the Wurstkranz (Strobl
# LevelComplete at 7916). Idle: tally, map Strobl -> Bad Ischl (Wait),
# intro, Bad Ischl play from 9028 still big. Bad Ischl (clock = frame -
# 9028): QA beam search, never hurt (the Kurgaeste, three officer files,
# the Fiaker, the first Traun notch; an extra life on the 100th Oblate),
# from 9970 (before notch 2) a hurt-free solver beam search, power kept,
# over the D-102 kerb and B2 pier to the goal (LevelComplete at 10897).
# Idle: tally, the map walk to Cafe Zauner, the map in Wait, the Cafe
# Zauner intro (11746) still big (score 58150, lives 4); the replay ends
# in the intro (11807). Re-cut for D-108 (M7): Stage 9 is playable now,
# so the map waits and leads into it instead of the teaser.
# Re-cut for D-102 (E42): Strobl's 230 s shorten its tally by 10 frames
# (10 idle frames fewer before Bad Ischl, whose inputs keep their clock);
# the old route ran into the kerb at 151; Bad Ischl's 210 s shorten its
# tally.
